-- `l4 run` EXITS 1 ON THIS FILE, BY DESIGN. Every #EVAL below names an assumed
-- term, so evaluation gets Stuck rather than producing a value, and a module
-- that cannot evaluate should not report success (ruled by Meng 2026-08-01; see
-- L4.Cli.Run.evalDirectiveCrashed). `l4 check` still exits 0 — the file is
-- well-typed, and that is the point of the example. If a quiet exit is ever
-- wanted, add a -q/--quiet-eval flag rather than flipping the default back.
-- The golden suite is unaffected: it evaluates in-process and compares output,
-- and never inspects a process exit code.

ASSUME foo IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO BOOLEAN
#EVAL foo 2

ASSUME bar IS A  BOOLEAN
baz b MEANS IF b THEN 2 ELSE 3
#EVAL baz bar
#EVAL IF bar THEN 2 ELSE 3
